# Release names, one line per release: "<VERSION>: <Name>". VERSION (next
# to this file) says which line is the release being built. A name is
# letters only: no accent, space, quote or digit, and it may be left empty
# until it is decided. os-release, lsb-release, issue, raye.info, the
# publish title, Raye Setup and GRUB say "Raye Linux <VERSION> <Name>",
# the name taking the place of a beta's number ("1.0 Beta 2: Sundog" is
# "Raye Linux 1.0 Beta Sundog"); the ISO file name and its volume label
# keep VERSION only.
#
# After changing a line, run tools/release_name.py --write and commit what
# it wrote (iso and installer): the image build refuses to start until
# every file says the same release (tools/release_name.py --check).
0.5 Beta: Alpenglow
1.0 Beta: Brocken
1.0 Beta 2: Sundog
1.1: Crepuscule
